# Local data exports — production dumps of customers/drivers/bookings land in
# scripts/ during migration and support work and carry emails, phone numbers,
# and names. Git history is effectively permanent, so a single `git add -A`
# would turn a local convenience into an unrecoverable PIPEDA disclosure.
# Blanket rule because a dump can be saved anywhere, not just scripts/.
# Already-tracked CSVs (Spinr_Code_Review_Matrix.csv) are unaffected — gitignore
# does not untrack. For a genuinely non-PII CSV, add it with `git add -f` and
# confirm it holds no personal data first.
*.csv

# Yarn drops install metadata into shared/ when resolving the file:../shared
# dependency from rider-app/driver-app — a local install byproduct, never source.
shared/.yarn-metadata.json
